## Development vs Production Architecture

### Development-Only Components

| Component             | Development                                     | Production                                    |
| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| **SQS Poller**        | Custom Node.js poller in Docker                 | Not deployed (uses AWS Event Source Mapping)   |
| **Dev Ack Simulator** | Standalone NestJS service (profile: `dev-tools`) | Not deployed (external system sends real ACKs) |
| **LocalStack**        | AWS services emulation                          | Not deployed (uses real AWS services)          |
| **Simulated Delays**  | Enabled via env var                             | Disabled (env var not set)                     |

### Production Components

| Component           | Purpose                      | Notes                                                   |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Orchestrator**    | Workflow coordination        | Same codebase, different env vars                       |
| **Lambda Workers**  | Input/Output step processing | Deployed to AWS Lambda (production) or LocalStack (dev) |
| **PostgreSQL**      | State persistence            | RDS (production) or Docker (dev)                        |
| **Kafka**           | Event streaming              | MSK (production) or Docker (dev)                        |
| **React Dashboard** | Monitoring UI                | S3+CloudFront (production) or local dev server (dev)    |

### Key Architectural Differences

**Development**:

```
API -> Orchestrator -> SQS (LocalStack) -> Custom Poller -> Lambda (LocalStack)
                                                            |
                                           CallbackService (Orchestrator)
                                                            |
                                           Kafka -> DevAckSimulator -> Kafka
                                                            |
                                           AcknowledgementHandler -> Continue
```

**Production**:

```
API -> Orchestrator -> SQS (AWS) -> Event Source Mapping -> Lambda (AWS)
                                                            |
                                           CallbackService (Orchestrator)
                                                            |
                                           Kafka -> External System -> Kafka
                                                            |
                                           AcknowledgementHandler -> Continue
```

**Critical**: `ENABLE_DEV_ACK_SIMULATOR` must be `false` or unset in production!

